Microsoft Learn: Protect Your Virtual Machines by Using Azure Backup

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Protect Your Virtual Machines by Using Azure Backup
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Beginner
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to use Azure Backup to protect Azure Virtual Machines, create backup policies, perform backup operations, and restore virtual machine data when recovery is required.

This module focused on implementing Azure Backup for Azure Virtual Machines, understanding backup scenarios, creating recovery points, and performing restore operations to support business continuity and disaster recovery.

Step 1: Understanding Azure Backup for Virtual Machines

The module introduced Azure Backup as a cloud-native backup service designed to protect Azure Virtual Machines and other workloads.

Azure Backup can protect:

Azure Virtual Machines
Azure Files
SQL Server databases
On-premises servers
Virtualized workloads
Primary goals:
Prevent data loss
Support disaster recovery
Enable rapid recovery
Meet compliance requirements
Benefits:
Automated backups
Secure storage
Centralized management
Long-term retention

The module emphasized that backup is a critical component of every production Azure environment.

Step 2: Understanding Azure Backup Scenarios

The training covered situations where Azure Backup should be used.

Common scenarios:
Accidental Deletion
User deletes important data
       ↓
Restore backup
Data Corruption
Application corruption
       ↓
Restore recovery point
Ransomware Attack
Files encrypted
       ↓
Restore clean backup
Infrastructure Failure
VM failure
       ↓
Recover VM
Key lesson learned:

Azure Backup protects against risks that high availability solutions cannot prevent.

Step 3: Understanding Recovery Services Vault

A major focus of the module was the Recovery Services Vault.

The Recovery Services Vault acts as the central backup management service.

Functions:
Stores backup metadata
Stores recovery points
Applies backup policies
Manages restore operations
Example:
Recovery Services Vault

├── VM Backups
├── Recovery Points
├── Backup Policies
└── Restore Jobs
Benefits:
Centralized management
Secure backup storage
Simplified administration

For AZ-104, remember:

Azure Backup requires a Recovery Services Vault.

