Key Takeaway

Azure Backup provides centralized, secure protection for Azure Virtual Machines and other workloads by creating recovery points that can be used to restore data after accidental deletion, corruption, ransomware attacks, or infrastructure failures. By implementing Recovery Services Vaults, backup policies, and restore procedures, Azure Administrators can build reliable backup strategies that support business continuity and disaster recovery. Understanding backup policies, recovery points, restore options, and Recovery Services Vaults is essential for the AZ-104 exam.
